      <h1>Data Deletion</h1>
      <p class="legal__date">Updated September 29, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="blog-post__body">
      <h2 id="request">Ask us to delete your data</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@vewo.ai">hello@vewo.ai</a> with the subject “Delete my data”. Tell us your name, your company and the email address you used with VEWO. We will confirm the request is yours, then:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>revoke and delete the access tokens for every account you connected, right away;</li>
        <li>delete your data from our systems within 30 days, except records the law requires us to keep, such as invoices;</li>
        <li>email you when it's done.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you are a customer of a business that uses VEWO, contact that business, or email us and we will pass the request to them.</p>

      <h2 id="disconnect">Disconnect an account yourself</h2>
      <p>You can remove VEWO's access at any time from each platform. Our access stops immediately.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Shopify</strong>: in your Shopify admin, open Settings, then Apps, and uninstall the VEWO app. Shopify then asks us to delete your store's data, and we do so within 30 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Facebook and Instagram</strong>: in Meta Business Settings, remove VEWO under Partners or Integrations, or in your Facebook settings open Business Integrations and remove VEWO.</li>
        <li><strong>Klaviyo</strong>: in Klaviyo, open Integrations and remove VEWO.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong>: visit <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">your Google Account's third-party access page</a> and remove VEWO.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Disconnecting stops new data from reaching VEWO. To delete what we already hold, email us as described above.</p>

      <h2 id="more">More detail</h2>
      <p>See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/dpa/">Data Processing Addendum</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
